    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe app derives read-only owner fields from the domain model and exposes them via an OpenAPI-generated DTO that MapStruct maps automatically by matching getter names (that's how `locality` already worked). So `timezone` needed two pieces:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `timezone` read-only string property to the `OwnerDto` schema (right after `locality`), documenting the fixed table. This generates the `timezone` field on `OwnerDto` at build time.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `REGION_TIMEZONE` table (`NSW->Australia/Sydney`, `VIC->Australia/Melbourne`, `QLD->Australia/Brisbane`) and a `getTimezone()` method that looks up `getLocality()` in that table, returning `null` when the locality isn't one of the three regions.\n\nMapStruct picks up `getTimezone()` \u2192 `timezone` with no explicit mapping, exactly like `getLocality()`. The acceptance test (`coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion`) now sees `$.locality == \"NSW\"` and `$.timezone == \"Australia/Sydney\"` for a Sydney owner.",
