    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change fits the established pattern in `Owner.java` exactly:\n\n- **Placement of the constant**: `REGION_TIMEZONE` sits alongside the sibling lookup tables `CITY_REGION` and `REGION_POSTCODE` (lines 96-118), with matching naming and the same `Map.of(...)` static-final idiom.\n- **Placement of the method**: `getTimezone()` is positioned immediately after `getLocality()` (the value it derives from), consistent with how this class groups a derived getter next to its dependency.\n- **Right unit / single source of truth**: deriving from `getLocality()` rather than re-deriving region from postcode/city reuses the existing canonical region accessor instead of duplicating the resolution logic \u2014 exactly what a maintainer here would expect.\n- **Consistency with the derived-getter family**: it joins `getAgeBand`, `getMembershipNumber`, `getContactPreference`, `getLocality`, etc. \u2014 small, pure, computed JavaBean getters with no stored column. Nothing is becoming a catch-all; `Owner` already owns this cluster of derived attributes.\n- **Documentation**: the Javadoc matches the surrounding style (summary, cross-references via `{@link}`, explicit null behavior, `@return`), and the OpenAPI `timezone` property mirrors the neighboring `locality`/`contactPreference` entries.\n\nNo duplication, logic is in the right place, and the structure reads naturally for this codebase.",
